: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Add the cycle test above; the mutation that removes the second record must make it fail.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T210000\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"A bypass the last review round raises is lost when the step blocks during that round's response, and a relaunch whose fresh reviewers miss it lets the gate pass\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `pasRelecture` (`cycle/src/cycle.ts`) records the bypasses a round leaves open (`ouverts`) only around the\n      response of a round that is not the last. When the last round raises a bypass, the response that writes the rest to\n      the registry runs before `clore` hands the bypass to the owner. If that response fails, or its commit turns\n      Preflight red, the step blocks with no record of the last round's bypass. On the relaunch, `depart` replays the\n      last round from the `ouverts` of the round before it; fresh reviewers that do not raise the bypass again let the\n      gate pass, and the step ends `fini`: the bypass is neither handed to the owner nor sent back to the red-green.\n    what_expected: >\n      A bypass a round raises is recorded before that round's response runs, so a relaunch after any block replays it,\n      whichever round raised it, including the single round that follows a reopening.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Drive the review step with the fake Claude: round 1 fixes an ordinary finding; at round 2, reviewer A raises a bypass and B a finding to weigh.\"\n      - \"Make the round 2 response fail, or commit a red test so Preflight stays red: the step blocks, gates [1 fail, 2 fail].\"\n      - \"Relaunch the step with reviewers that raise nothing: it ends `fini` with gate [2 pass].\"\n    root_cause: >\n      What a round raised is kept in memory until its response is done; only the round before the last writes it to the\n      journal, and nothing persists the last round